docs/media/final and docs/media/rf hold renders of LAFAN1 motions (© 2018 Ubisoft Entertainment; CC BY-NC-ND 4.0;
https://github.com/ubisoft/ubisoft-laforge-animation-dataset), retargeted to the G1 (LAFAN1 Retargeting Dataset),
resampled, cut to 10 s and rendered. They are for non-commercial illustration only and are not covered by the MIT
license in LICENSE.

docs/media/boxing holds a render of InterHuman clip 1566 (https://github.com/tr3e/InterGen; CC BY-NC-SA 4.0), both people
retargeted to the G1 with HoloRetarget and rendered. It is shared under CC BY-NC-SA 4.0
(https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/) and is not covered by the MIT license in LICENSE.

docs/media/musclevae holds renders of policies tracking the walk and run clips of MuscleVAE
(https://github.com/wangchek/MuscleVAE_, whose repository has no license): LAFAN1 motions (© 2018 Ubisoft Entertainment;
CC BY-NC-ND 4.0) retargeted to its skeleton, drawn with the bone meshes of MASS (https://github.com/lsw9021/MASS;
Apache-2.0). They are for non-commercial illustration only and are not covered by the MIT license in LICENSE.

docs/media/hand holds renders of a policy tracking SPIDER's kinematic retargets
(https://huggingface.co/datasets/retarget/retarget_full) of hand-object demonstrations from HRDexDB, OakInk and DexYCB,
with the retargets drawn over it, those datasets' object meshes and the XHand's model. They are for non-commercial
illustration only and are not covered by the MIT license in LICENSE.

docs/media/robokit holds renders of RoboKit's (https://github.com/openrobokit/robokit; MIT) G1 box carrying, G1 climbing and
Go2 jumping examples, planned on this library's world model and executed in MuJoCo Warp, with Unitree's G1 model
(BSD-3-Clause) and MuJoCo Menagerie's Unitree Go2 (https://github.com/google-deepmind/mujoco_menagerie; BSD-3-Clause). The G1
climbing render tracks a climbing motion capture of OmniRetarget / Holosoma (https://github.com/amazon-far/holosoma;
Apache-2.0). The G1 box carrying render (g1_carry.webp) tracks a clip of OMOMO (https://github.com/lijiaman/omomo_release, whose
data terms are not stated) that RoboKit retargets; it is for non-commercial illustration only and is not covered by the MIT
license in LICENSE.

docs/media/teaser.webp puts 6 s of such renders in a row: its LAFAN1 tracking column under the first paragraph's terms,
its Two G1s column under CC BY-NC-SA 4.0 as in the second, its Muscles column under the third's, its Hand-object column
under the fourth's, and its second row, the docs/media/robokit renders, with the sources and terms that paragraph names.
No part of it is covered by the MIT license in LICENSE.
